id: pm-x3dq0l
title: "GH-954: fail-fast dependency target validation with explicit forward-reference intent"
description: Reject unresolved dependency targets during create/update unless the caller explicitly opts into a forward reference; keep graph truth and repair semantics discoverable.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-09T22:12:19.846Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T08:53:29.092Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#f40a3612ddfb4cf32376b325"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: Create and update reject unresolved dependency ids by default; an explicit allow-unresolved contract records intentional forward references; help SDK contracts MCP and completions expose additive replacement removal and forward-reference semantics; structured recovery names search dep-remove replace-deps and clear-deps; tests cover create update bulk and transaction paths
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make dependency writes referentially truthful by default
value: Agents receive immediate recovery instead of silently corrupting the graph
why_now: GitHub #954 demonstrates that the accepted-forward-reference decision in pm-ol5v remains unsafe and combines with strict relationship policy
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
expected_result: Unresolved dependency writes require explicit intent
actual_result: Current create and update silently persist unresolved ids
